From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:00:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] pmdomain: qcom: cpr: let the MSM8926 sleep set request MX
 retention

The CPR sleep guard keeps the sleep-only MX vote (l3-so) at the 1.2875 V
ceiling, so the RPM never reaches VDD-min. The RPM applies the sleep
set only after the whole APSS cluster has collapsed and restores the
active set, where CPR keeps MX at its ceiling through l3-ao, before it
releases the cluster. The stock kernel votes 8226_l3_so at 750 mV
permanently. Lower the sleep-only vote to 750 mV after a successful
suspend prepare and raise it back first when restoring.

Assisted-by: LLM [Claude Code]
---
 drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr-msm8926-suspend.h | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr-msm8926-suspend.h b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr-msm8926-suspend.h
index 1b5cead8b..b3befc4d9 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr-msm8926-suspend.h
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr-msm8926-suspend.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "cpr-voltage.h"
 
 #define CPR_SUSPEND_SAFE_RATE	300000000UL
+#define CPR_SUSPEND_MX_RETENTION_UV	750000
 #define CPR_SUSPEND_CFG_MASK	(GENMASK(10, 8) | GENMASK(4, 0))
 #define CPR_SUSPEND_CMD_BUSY	(BIT(0) | BIT(4) | BIT(31))
 
@@ -95,7 +96,10 @@ static inline int cpr_suspend_cover(struct cpr_msm8926_suspend *sleep)
 	ret = cpr_suspend_sync(rails->mx);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	/* Retain the covering sleep ceiling; lowering it needs a separate proof. */
+	/* Raise the sleep-set MX vote back to the covering ceiling first. */
+	ret = regulator_set_voltage(sleep->sleep_mx, rails->mx_max_uV, rails->mx_max_uV);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 	ret = cpr_suspend_sync(sleep->sleep_mx);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
@@ -209,6 +213,18 @@ static inline int cpr_suspend_prepare(struct cpr_msm8926_suspend *sleep,
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 		goto restore;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * The RPM applies the sleep set only once every APSS core and the L2
+	 * have collapsed, and restores the active set (MX at the l3-ao ceiling)
+	 * before it releases the cluster. Like the stock 8226_l3_so vote, let
+	 * the sleep set request MX retention so the RPM can enter VDD-min.
+	 */
+	ret = regulator_set_voltage(sleep->sleep_mx, CPR_SUSPEND_MX_RETENTION_UV,
+				    rails->mx_max_uV);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = cpr_suspend_sync(sleep->sleep_mx);
+	if (ret)
+		goto restore;
 	return 0;
 
 restore:
